Z||000000||Richard Parnell||04-10-2001||01:10 PM||||As some of you know I wrecked my Fiero last week.  Got the new fender, fascia and hood on.  The problem (among others) is the headlights I got are different from mt 87 .  The connector is different and there are thre wires going to the motor unit instead of two.  Can I still use these motors?||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||04-10-2001||01:16 PM||||87 was year they went to completly different system.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||04-10-2001||07:09 PM||||you have the gen 1 motors on the replacement parts. If you can salvage you original motor put it on this lift assembly. I won't know if or how the old motor could be adapted to work with the Gen 2 87+ system.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Richard Parnell||04-10-2001||11:10 PM||||Thanks Ogre, I did manage to salvage the old motors and mounted them in the older housings which were the same as the '87.  I got the car back together, although I still need to make some adjustments to the body parts I replaced.  The lights amazingly went up on the first try after aboout 5-7 tries on adjusting the hood.  Had to "readjust w/5lb. hammer)" the bent portion of the frame that holds the hood hinge.<BR> I can tell now how much the front area of the car is bent.  It's not too far off but unless I pull all the front and chain the car to a tree, it'll never be show quality with the car being perfect, but you know I just don't care. I just plain like my car, warts and all. I thought I'd be more upset about the wreck than I was.  I actually had fun  working on the car and it really wasn't that tough, unless you count getting up off your A** a chore, which I sometimes do.  Well thanks for the advice. I do have some questions about the guages and some other electrical odd things that are happening on my car since I got rid of the ecm for the V8 conversion.||||reg||7
